# The look the legibility gate scores (PBR text T13, organon#217) — `faceplate`, as far
# as the `organon` CLI can set it, plus the three departures the gate itself needs.
#
# Read by `verify.sh --legibility` with the same rules as `verify/scenes/*.scene`: one
# `organon` command per line, `#` comments and blank lines ignored, shell-style quoting.
# There are no `#!` directives here — this is not a golden scene; the judge is
# `legibility-gate` against `thresholds.toml`, and the fixture is
# `organon-render/tests/fixtures/omarchy-logo.txt` with its colours taken from the ring.
#
# ⚠️ THIS IS NOT THE WHOLE PRESET. `preset.rs::builtin_text_presets()` is the authority
# for `faceplate`; the harness runs the visual with no writer, so a preset cannot be
# recalled, and only ids on the vocabulary (`organon-agent::ACTUATABLE_IDS`) can be set.
# Nine of the rung's fields are not on it and stay at the visual's defaults here:
#   atmos_enabled=false  bg_visible=false      (the dark room — the sky stays behind the grid;
#                                               it is outside the cells and the gate ignores it)
#   fx_enabled=true      hal_amount=0.35       (halation — the CRT post pass stays off)
#   ml_enabled=true      ml_intensity=1.0      ml_radius=2.0  ml_count=64  ml_restir=false
#                                              (glyphs as lights — the pools on the backplane
#                                               are not in this frame)
# So the gate scores the faceplate TILES under the faceplate RIG, without its halation and
# without its pools. Registering those ids (seven sites, per the CLI-vocab change) or a
# harness that runs the standalone and recalls the preset would close the gap; until then
# the README says which half is measured.
#
# The three departures, deliberate:
#   glyph_cam_tilt 0   — the preset tilts 6°; the gate's grid geometry is axis-aligned
#                        (`GridGeom` has no homography), so the gate render is straight on.
#   glyph_margin 0     — the rig fits the backplane's bounds to the frame, margin included;
#                        with no margin the GRID fills the frame along one axis, which is
#                        the case `fit` handles and the case `auto` refines from.
#   rot_mod_* 0 etc.   — the clock, frozen the way every golden scene freezes it; the held
#                        camera bypasses the orbit, but a moving generator field behind a
#                        ring that goes silent would still be a moving picture.

generator "organic math"
surface original
material clearcoat

set rot_mod_x 0 rot_mod_y 0 rot_mod_z 0
set rot_amp_x 0 rot_amp_y 0 rot_amp_z 0
set trans_amp_x 0 trans_amp_y 0 trans_amp_z 0
set scale_amp 0
set cam_path 0 cam_speed 0 cam_kick 0

# The tiles (T3): bevel and crown, over the near-black dielectric under a thin coat.
set glyph_bevel 0.12 glyph_crown 0.35
set metallic 0 roughness 0.22

# The held, fitted camera — straight on for the gate (the preset says 6).
set glyph_cam_hold 1 glyph_cam_tilt 0 glyph_cam_zoom 1
set glyph_margin 0

# The room: the IBL dimmed to a faint sheen (the atmosphere and background toggles are
# not on the vocabulary — see the header).
set env_intensity 0.15

# The rig (T10): a key from low on the right, a faint fill.
set key_intensity 1.6 fill_intensity 0.25 elevation 15 azimuth 70
